{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"05825198-5d0b-4b21-8a0f-2a7ef565ccbd","title":"The complement of an event in a Venn diagram"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"05825198-5d0b-4b21-8a0f-2a7ef565ccbd","step":{"id":"s1","script":"The rectangle represents every possible outcome, called the sample space. The circle represents event A: the outcomes where A happens.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Complement of an event"},{"op":"figure","id":"venn","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4.5,4.5],"y":[-3,3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"sample","points":[[-4,-2.5],[4,-2.5],[4,2.5],[-4,2.5]],"closed":true},{"kind":"circle","id":"event","center":[0,0],"r":1.5},{"kind":"text","at":[-3.5,2],"text":"S"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0],"text":"A"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"sampledef","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"S = \\text{all possible outcomes}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"05825198-5d0b-4b21-8a0f-2a7ef565ccbd","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The complement of A contains every outcome in the sample space that is not in A. Shade outside the circle, but inside the rectangle.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"shading","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"shade","inside":"sample","except":["event"]},{"kind":"text","at":[2.7,0],"text":"not A"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"sampledef","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"A^c = S\\setminus A"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"05825198-5d0b-4b21-8a0f-2a7ef565ccbd","step":{"id":"s3","script":"An outcome is either in A or in its complement, never both. Together, these two regions contain all the probability.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"outcomes","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":[0.5,0.5],"label":"in A"},{"kind":"point","at":[-2.7,-1],"label":"in Aᶜ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"total","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(A)+P(A^c)=1"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"total","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\boxed{P(A^c)=1-P(A)}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If P(A) = 0.3, what is the probability of the shaded complement?","expected_gist":"0.7, because 1 minus 0.3 equals 0.7."}}}
